+	 * corrupt, and anything this code loads through a pointer can fault,
+	 * which raises ANOTHER double exception and lands back at the vector.
+	 * So: if the magic is already set we are that second fault -- keep the
+	 * first record and spin. Otherwise store the special registers (which
+	 * cannot fault), write the magic, and only then attempt the two loads
+	 * through the CPU struct, flagging them separately if they succeed.
+	 */
